@startuml
actor User
participant FE
participant BE
participant DB

User -> FE : Click download on file

FE -> BE : GET /files/{id}
BE -> BE : Validate JWT
BE -> DB : Fetch file record\n(\n  ciphertext,\n  wrapped_FEK,\n  nonce,\n  auth_tag,\n  stored_hash,\n  enc_algo,\n  hash_algo\n)
DB --> BE : encrypted file data
BE --> FE : encrypted file data

note over FE : All decryption happens\nclient-side only — server\nnever sees plaintext or raw FEK

FE -> FE : Prompt user for password
FE -> FE : Derive key from password\n(PBKDF2 + stored salt)
FE -> FE : Decrypt private key blob\n→ RSA key object
FE -> FE : Unwrap FEK using RSA\nprivate key (OAEP)\n→ raw 32-byte FEK
FE -> FE : Decrypt ciphertext using FEK + nonce\n(AES-256-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305)
FE -> FE : Verify auth tag\n→ confirms ciphertext was not tampered with

FE -> FE : Recompute hash of decrypted plaintext\nusing stored hash_algo\n(SHA-256 / SHA-512 / MD5)
FE -> FE : Compare recomputed hash\nvs stored hash

alt hashes match
    FE --> User : Plaintext file\n+ INTEGRITY PASS (hashes match)
else hashes differ
    FE --> User : WARNING — integrity FAILED\nFile may have been tampered with
end
@enduml